  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-oriented-slope-and-knot-dehn-filling": [
      "## Definition\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere, let $N(K)$ be a chosen closed tubular solid-torus neighborhood, let $E_K=\\overline{S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)}$, and let $T_K=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$. Let $\\mu$ be the positive oriented meridian, meaning the boundary of a positive normal disk in $N(K)$, and let $\\lambda$ be a preferred longitude, meaning a degree-one parallel of the core $K$ in $N(K)$ that is null-homologous in $E_K$. Assume that $[\\mu],[\\lambda]$ are an ordered basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$, with the boundary-orientation convention $\\mu\\cdot\\lambda=-1$. A slope is the unoriented isotopy class of an essential simple closed curve on $T_K$ whose homology class is $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$ for coprime integers $p,q$ not both zero; $(p,q)$ and $(-p,-q)$ represent the same slope. For a slope represented by $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$, the Dehn filling $E_K(p/q)$ is obtained by gluing an oriented solid torus $D^2\\times S^1$ to $E_K$ by an orientation-reversing boundary homeomorphism that sends $[\\partial D^2\\times\\{1\\}]$ to that slope; the filled orientation agrees with the fixed orientation on $E_K$. If $q\\ne0$, the coefficient is written $p/q$; the meridional slope is $1/0$, and integer $n$-framed filling means slope $n[\\mu]+[\\lambda]$. The oriented homeomorphism type is independent of the gluing map once its meridian image is fixed."
    ],
    "lem-knot-surgery-first-homology-mayer-vietoris": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere with a chosen connected exterior $E_K$ and boundary torus $T_K$. Let $(\\mu,\\lambda)$ be its positive meridian and preferred longitude, assume $([\\mu],[\\lambda])$ is a basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$, and assume $[\\mu]$ generates $H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)$ and $[\\lambda]=0$. For coprime integers $p,q$ not both zero, let $E_K(p/q)$ be the filling whose attached solid-torus meridian maps to $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$. Then\n$$H_1(E_K(p/q);\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\begin{cases}\\mathbb Z/|p|\\mathbb Z,&p\\ne0,\\\\[2pt]\\mathbb Z,&p=0.\\end{cases}$$"
    ],
    "thm-framed-knot-surgery-trace-boundary": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere with a chosen exterior $E_K$ and peripheral basis $(\\mu,\\lambda)$, where $\\lambda$ is preferred. For $n\\in\\mathbb Z$, attach one smooth $4$-dimensional $2$-handle $D^2\\times D^2$ to the $4$-ball $B^4$ along $S^1\\times D^2$ in $\\partial B^4=S^3$ by the standard orientation-compatible handle attachment, using a product framing whose attaching parallel on $\\partial E_K$ has slope $n[\\mu]+[\\lambda]$. Denote the resulting oriented trace by $X_n(K)$. After rounding corners, its oriented boundary is the filling $E_K(n/1)$. This theorem covers integer framings only: a rational $p/q$ filling has a trace only after specifying an integral continued-fraction handle chain or a separately defined rational-surgery cobordism; an arbitrary rational coefficient is not the framing of a single smooth $2$-handle."
    ],
    "def-lens-space-surgery-orientation-convention": [
      "## Definition\n\nAssume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. An oriented lens space is an oriented closed $3$-manifold obtained by gluing two solid tori by an orientation-reversing boundary homeomorphism. For coprime integers $p>0$ and $q$, let $L(p,q)$ denote the oriented union of the exterior of the unknot in the oriented $3$-sphere and a solid torus whose meridian is identified with the slope $p[\\mu_U]+q[\\lambda_U]$ on the unknot exterior. Thus this library uses the convention $L(p,q)=E_U(p/q)$; no symbol $L(0,q)$ is assigned."
    ],
    "lem-trefoil-plus-one-surgery-group-presentation": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $T$ be the closure of the positive geometric two-strand braid $\\sigma_1^3$, with orientation given by increasing braid parameter. In the chart $(x,y,t)$ with ambient orientation $(x,y,t)$, view along $+y$, put increasing $t$ downward, and orient the projection plane by $(\\partial_t,\\partial_x)$. The right-starting strand passes over the left-starting strand at each positive crossing. Let $E_T$ be its chosen exterior. For the positive meridian $\\mu=a$ at the first left arc and the preferred degree-one longitude $\\lambda$, the fundamental group of $+1$ filling, with slope $[\\mu]+[\\lambda]$, has presentation\n$$\\pi_1(E_T(1/1))\\cong\\langle a,b\\mid aba=bab,\\;bab^{-1}aba^{-2}=1\\rangle.$$\nIn these based coordinates the blackboard parallel is $w=bac$ with $c=b^{-1}ab$, and\n$$w a^3=(ab)^3,\\qquad\\lambda=w a^{-3}=(ab)^3a^{-6}.$$\nThus the same filling relation is $(ab)^3=a^5$. In particular the positive trefoil and the sign of the filling are both fixed; no mirror substitution is implicit."
    ],
